Use correctly configured UV mapping.

Ensure texture colors remain consistent with the renderer's color-space settings.

Avoid extreme texture stretching.

When procedural textures are generated through CanvasTexture, ensure the texture data can actually be embedded in the GLB export.

Do not use dynamic shader effects as a substitute for permanent material information when those effects cannot be exported reliably.

### Material discipline

Use export-compatible standard or unlit materials where appropriate.

Avoid unsupported custom shaders for permanent room assets.

Preview-specific visual effects must remain separate from the exported material data.

